@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Dictionary search and exact text handoff — no Collection write
hide footbox
autonumber
actor Visitor
participant "Dictionary / App\n<<browser functions>>" as UI
participant "backend.dictionary\n<<route-target functions>>" as Dictionary
participant "compiler.lexer.reference\n<<functions>>" as Reference
database "Bundled Markdown\nlegacy senses" as Files
activate Visitor
Visitor -> UI : search words and select a result page
activate UI
UI -> Dictionary : GET /api/dictionary?query=...&offset=...&limit=...
activate Dictionary
note over Dictionary : FastAPI public read routing/limit precedes list_dictionary().
Dictionary -> Dictionary : load_dictionary()
activate Dictionary
Dictionary -> Reference : load_classified_lexicon()
activate Reference
Reference --> Dictionary : immutable supplied ReferenceEntry rows (cached)
deactivate Reference
Dictionary -> Files : read camfranglais.md and extra_lexicon.md
activate Files
Files --> Dictionary : Markdown source text, or read error
deactivate Files
note over Dictionary : parse_dictionary() retains source lines.\nMerge supplied rows with legacy senses not already supplied.
Dictionary --> Dictionary : DictionaryEntry list, or CollectionError(503)
deactivate Dictionary
note over Dictionary : Normalize search words, require every word to match,\nthen page matches and retain all source filenames.
Dictionary --> UI : DictionaryResponse, or explicit error
deactivate Dictionary
UI --> Visitor : source-labelled senses, counts and pagination
deactivate UI
Visitor -> UI : copy selected reference text to Franc Analyzer
activate UI
UI -> UI : openCompiler(text, "dictionary")\nin App.tsx
activate UI
UI --> UI : exact incoming text with reference provenance
deactivate UI
UI --> Visitor : draft only; Analyze must be selected to retain a test
deactivate UI
deactivate Visitor
legend bottom
  Dictionary reference data is not Collection and is not evidence of human collection.
  The UI handoff sends no POST and never inserts a Collection entry.
  The 938-entry merged dictionary is a dated source snapshot, not a test count or fieldwork result.
endlegend
@enduml
